@startuml
title Ticketera Municipal - despliegue separado

node "Navegador / App del vecino" as ClienteVecino {
    artifact "WebApp (SPA)" as artWebApp
}

node "Equipo del operador municipal" as ClienteMunicipal {
    artifact "PanelMunicipal (SPA)" as artPanel
}

node "Sistema externo" as ClienteSoap {
    artifact "Cliente SOAP\n(integracion)" as artSoap
}

node "Servidor Docker Host\n(docker-compose.yml, red bridge del proyecto)" as DockerHost {

    node "Contenedor: reclamos\nHTTP 8080" as ReclamosContainer {
        artifact "ticketera-reclamos.jar (Spring Boot)\nAuth, Ciudadanos, Reclamos, Cuadrillas,\nSOAP, Nominatim y ConsumidorCuadrillas" as artReclamos
    }

    node "Contenedor: ia\nHTTP 8081" as IAContainer {
        artifact "ticketera-ia.jar (Spring Boot)\nResumenes, ranking, duplicados,\nGemini y ConsumidorIA\ncache en memoria" as artIA
    }

    node "Contenedor: postgres" as PgContainer {
        database "PostgreSQL 16\n(base compartida)" as artDB
    }

    node "Contenedor: rabbitmq" as MqContainer {
        artifact "RabbitMQ 3\n(exchange + colas + DLQ)" as artMq
    }

    node "Contenedor: redis" as RedisContainer {
        database "Redis 7\n(reservado, sin uso)" as artRedis
    }
}

cloud "Proveedor de LLM" as NodoLLM {
    artifact "API Gemini" as artLLM
}

cloud "Proveedor de Geolocalizacion" as NodoGeo {
    artifact "API Nominatim / OSM" as artGeo
}

note bottom of ReclamosContainer
  JWT_SECRET compartido; login emite el token.
  Secretos por entorno, sin claves en las imagenes.
  Healthchecks de PostgreSQL/RabbitMQ antes del arranque.
  Modo integrado alternativo en diagrama 05a.
end note

note bottom of IAContainer
  Valida JWT y exige ADMIN para el resumen.
  LLM_API_KEY llega solo a este contenedor.
  Eventos persistentes por RabbitMQ.
end note

note bottom of PgContainer
  Volumen nombrado postgres_data
end note

note bottom of MqContainer
  Volumen nombrado rabbitmq_data
end note

ClienteVecino --> ReclamosContainer : HTTP 8080\n(REST JSON)
ClienteMunicipal --> ReclamosContainer : HTTP 8080\n(REST JSON + JWT)
ClienteMunicipal --> IAContainer : HTTP 8081\n(resumen + JWT)
ClienteSoap --> ReclamosContainer : HTTP 8080\n(SOAP /ws, WSDL /ws/reclamos.wsdl)

ReclamosContainer --> PgContainer : JDBC 5432
IAContainer --> PgContainer : JDBC 5432
ReclamosContainer <--> MqContainer : AMQP 5672
IAContainer <--> MqContainer : AMQP 5672
IAContainer ..> RedisContainer : reservado\n(sin conexion actual)
IAContainer --> NodoLLM : HTTPS (API REST)
ReclamosContainer --> NodoGeo : HTTPS (API REST)
@enduml
